  "response": "To start the Ollama container with access to all NVIDIA GPUs, you need to configure Docker to use the NVIDIA driver and then run the container with specific options. Here's how you can do it based on the provided context:\n\n1. **Configure Docker to use the NVIDIA driver:**\n\n   You need to ensure Docker is set up to use the NVIDIA driver. Run the following commands:\n\n   ```shell\n   sudo nvidia-ctk runtime configure --runtime=docker\n   sudo systemctl restart docker\n   ```\n\n2. **Start the Ollama container with GPU access:**\n\n   Use the following command to start the Ollama container, ensuring it has access to all NVIDIA GPUs:\n\n   ```shell\n   docker run -d --gpus=all -v ollama:/root/.ollama -p 11434:11434 --name ollama ollama/ollama\n   ```\n\n   - The `--gpus=all` option allows the container to access all available NVIDIA GPUs.\n   - The `-v ollama:/root/.ollama` option mounts a volume to persist data.\n   - The `-p 11434:11434` option maps port 11434 from the container to the host.\n   - The `--name ollama` option names the container \"ollama\".\n\nEnsure that the NVIDIA drivers and Docker are properly installed and configured on your system. If you encounter any issues, refer to the troubleshooting steps provided in the context for additional guidance.",
